f-balls-field","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to torn Achilles","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich sustained a torn right Achilles tendon in Saturday's win against SMU, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-22T23:15:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50566676/notre-dame-loses-safety-luke-talich-torn-achilles","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What Week 12's unexpected results mean for Rivalry Week and beyond","description":"After another chaotic weekend, we look at the playoff and conference races on the line with one game to go.","published":"2026-11-22T23:54:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563018/week-12-results-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 recruit AJ Randle Jr. flips from Miami to Notre Dame","description":"Notre Dame coach Marcus Freeman flipped Miami pledge AJ Randle Jr., ESPN's No. 9 outside linebacker in the 2027 recruiting class, to fill a late-cycle need.","published":"2026-11-22T22:48:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50565158/2027-recruit-aj-randle-jr-flips-miami-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pac-12 reveals unique flex schedule for season's final week","description":"The Pac-12 announced its unique flex schedule for the final week of the regular season early Sunday morning.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564960/pac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest rewards DC Scottie Hazelton with contract extension","description":"Wake Forest defensive coordinator Scottie Hazelton has signed a contract extension.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564902/wake-forest-rewards-dc-scottie-hazelton-extension","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4702828/aj-holmes-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._J._Holmes_Jr."},"pick":{"pick":41,"round":2,"team":"ATL","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"A. J. Holmes Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._J._Holmes_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:12Z","intro":"Anthony \"A. J.\" Holmes Jr. (born November 7, 2003) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. He previously played for the Houston Cougars.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Holmes Jr. attended Westfield High School in Houston, Texas. As a senior season, he was named the District 14-6A MVP. Coming out of high school, Holmes Jr. committed to play college football for the Houston Cougars over other offers from schools such as TCU, Kansas State, Washington State, SMU, and Virginia."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"HOUSTON\nDuring his freshman season in 2022, Holmes Jr. notched six tackles with half a tackle being for a loss. In the 2023 season, he appeared in 12 games with three starts, where he totaled 21 tackles with four and a half going for a loss, and two and a half sacks. During the 2024 season, Holmes Jr. tallied 40 tackles with eight and a half being for a loss, and two sacks. After the season, he entered his name into the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS TECH\nHolmes Jr. transferred to play for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. In week 2 of the 2025 season, he notched four tackles with two being for a loss, a sack, a pass deflection, and a fumble recovery in a blowout win over Kent State. In week 6, Holmes Jr. recorded two sacks in a win versus Kansas. In week 7, he recorded a sack against Arizona State. For his performance during the 2025 season, Holmes Jr. was named a first-team All-American by Pro Football Focus."}]}}